Working out what is actually wrong	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The reported problem is rarely the real one"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A customer writes to say the portal is broken. In practice that sentence covers a forgotten password, an expired card, a genuine outage, and an order that shipped to an old address. Treat the opening message as a symptom, not a diagnosis."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three questions that resolve most of it"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What were you trying to do when it happened?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What did you expect to see, and what did you see instead?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "When did it last work?"}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask all three at once rather than one per reply. Every round trip costs the customer half a day and makes them angrier than the original fault did."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check the account before you ask. Half the time the answer is already in the order history, and asking a question you could have answered yourself reads as not caring."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "1167b7be-cc14-596d-bd71-d8f7e2f7d51a", "questions": [{"question_id": "4d6271b7-110f-5c45-8174-f5e6eb6f4c20", "question": "What should you do before asking a customer for more detail?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "8269494e-48e5-5e5b-b363-cc8b2123d238", "answer": "Check their account and order history first", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "876bb110-f213-52e5-a698-3d5490023530", "answer": "Ask them to restate the problem more clearly", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "d00621bf-9377-5497-88f6-48914c2ea428", "answer": "Escalate to the account owner", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	73	2	21	activity_9eed496c-5212-42a7-b3c0-6a019726ad9f	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.321417	null	1	\N
Writing the first reply	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Acknowledge, state, commit"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The first reply does three jobs: it shows a human read the message, it says what you now understand the problem to be, and it commits to a next step with a time attached. Everything else can wait for the second reply."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Acknowledge the actual inconvenience, not a generic apology for any inconvenience caused."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Restate the problem in your own words so they can correct you if you have it wrong."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what happens next and when. 'I will come back to you by end of day Thursday' is a commitment; 'I will look into it' is not."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never say this"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Avoid telling a customer the system is working as intended. It may be true and it is never useful \\u2014 it tells someone with a problem that their problem is not going to be solved. Describe what you can do instead."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "048910d0-677f-5ecf-9e7f-6f3b4199e287", "questions": [{"question_id": "a4a226a8-bd0f-54ca-9463-5cfa381ba7c0", "question": "Which of these is a real commitment in a first reply?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "57c394e6-c3e4-525a-aa1a-be35e9b4f3c6", "answer": "I will come back to you by end of day Thursday", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "a0f04de7-06c4-5d53-a3ee-f8c1b726e77c", "answer": "I will look into this and get back to you", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "72103484-51db-5f23-a7de-156df1000b00", "answer": "This is working as intended", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	74	2	21	activity_d0dcca3f-cac4-46c5-aa40-0390194bf5fd	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.324127	null	1	\N
Deciding what is urgent	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Urgency is about consequence, not volume"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The loudest message is not the most urgent one. Sort by what happens if you leave it until tomorrow: a customer who cannot receive a delivery they have already paid for outranks a customer asking for a feature, however forcefully."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Blocked and paid: they have given us money and cannot get what they bought. Today."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Blocked and unpaid: they cannot complete a purchase. Today if you can."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Degraded: it works, badly, and there is a workaround. This week."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Wishlist: it does not do a thing they want. Log it and say so honestly."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Anything affecting more than one customer at once stops being a support ticket and becomes an incident. Say so in the team channel immediately rather than working through them one at a time."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	75	2	21	activity_e78395cd-2699-4a3d-92b6-3010ba37db99	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.326734	null	1	\N
When the customer is angry	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It is almost never about you"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "By the time someone is angry at support, they have usually already lost time, been passed around, or explained themselves twice. The anger belongs to the situation. Answering it defensively puts you in the argument; answering the problem takes you out of it."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What actually reduces the temperature"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Name what went wrong, specifically. Vague sympathy reads as a brush-off."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Take the next step yourself rather than telling them who to contact."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Give a time and then beat it. Nothing rebuilds trust faster than an update arriving before it was promised."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What does not help: matching their tone, over-apologising, or explaining our internal process. The customer does not care which team owns the fault, and telling them makes it sound like an excuse."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If a message is genuinely abusive rather than angry, you are not required to absorb it. Hand it to your team lead and say why."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "223e261e-e3a6-5012-a3d5-13a8a07fc9f6", "questions": [{"question_id": "5be009eb-dedf-57da-869f-ab76a5731aca", "question": "A customer is angry after being passed between two teams. What helps most?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "7244b9f1-6fc0-5b9f-be6b-120d6d9806da", "answer": "Taking the next step yourself instead of redirecting them again", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "9b8e53ef-11d9-5c84-a1f0-2686b2b99e81", "answer": "Explaining which team is responsible for the delay", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "5d51a448-4afe-5660-9c17-a724066bd1f7", "answer": "Apologising repeatedly for the inconvenience", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	76	2	21	activity_77494d39-3155-4fd3-8f78-d11f15adef43	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.332070	null	1	\N
Compliance assessment	TYPE_ASSIGNMENT	SUBTYPE_ASSIGNMENT_ANY	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Required annually"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Six scenarios drawn from things that have actually happened: a misdirected email, a supplier changing bank details, a data request arriving in a support chat, an access question, a threshold decision, and a request to skip a step under time pressure."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "For each, say what you would do and in what order. The reporting timings and the verification step for payment details are the parts that must be right \\u2014 the rest is marked on reasoning."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	108	2	24	activity_7d5fe6aa-5fab-4b6b-af87-113aa504f795	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.475724	null	1	\N
What your first week looks like	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The week is deliberately quiet"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Nobody expects output from you this week. The work is to build a map: of the company, of your team, and of where things are written down. People who rush past this stage spend their second month asking questions they could have answered in week one."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What is already booked"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Monday: a welcome session with your manager, and your accounts switched on."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Tuesday and Wednesday: shadowing whoever does the job closest to yours."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Thursday: a walk through the product with someone from the support team."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Friday: a half-hour with your manager to say what is still confusing."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Everything else is yours to fill. If a day looks empty, that is on purpose \\u2014 use it to read, to poke at the product, and to write down what does not make sense yet."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep a running list of things that confused you. It is the most useful document you will ever write here, and it expires within a month."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "18beee04-e555-572d-a072-60659f5fac9f", "questions": [{"question_id": "ef842ff3-d19d-5030-9477-b9fefd04ba05", "question": "What is the main goal of your first week?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "b7b44abb-d1ee-5336-86ff-7cc341d1a3f3", "answer": "Building a map of the company, the team and the documentation", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "28b33de5-239c-5042-b3e1-75069da38b0f", "answer": "Shipping your first piece of work", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "d750cb63-438b-5e51-9104-4bc869542b0a", "answer": "Meeting every single person in the company", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	55	2	19	activity_d5b3699a-1aaf-4541-ab00-536d2d719de4	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.213554	null	1	\N
Who does what	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four groups, and what they own"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Riverbend is small enough that you will eventually know everyone, and large enough that you will not manage it this month. Start with the four groups you will actually deal with."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Supply: decides what we stock and what it costs. Ask them anything about availability."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Accounts: owns the relationship with each customer, including the awkward conversations about money."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Support: answers customers directly, and knows more about how the product really behaves than anyone."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Operations: keeps the warehouse and the deliveries honest. If a date is at risk, they know first."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The rule of thumb"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If a question is about what we sell, ask Supply. If it is about a specific customer, ask whoever owns that account. If it is about something that broke, ask Support before you guess. Nobody minds being asked; everybody minds finding out late."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "304ef636-fbdf-5335-8423-2c277f8931da", "questions": [{"question_id": "675d5dd3-7118-5fa5-ad2b-399203b1d0b8", "question": "A customer asks whether an item will be back in stock next month. Who do you ask first?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "98fbcb0b-10e9-5b59-a39f-e5b0417b592f", "answer": "Supply", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "70a7b738-2d49-53ac-96c4-9e2731d0b929", "answer": "Operations", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "b0eca55b-58f8-5626-8b08-256897a61857", "answer": "Accounts", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	56	2	19	activity_116731f2-2358-4467-9010-0117657cde17	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.223989	null	1	\N
Setting up your tools	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do these four things today"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Sign in to every account in your welcome email, and turn on two-factor authentication while you are there."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Add yourself to the shared team calendar so people can see when you are free."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Set a profile photo and a real name. It matters more than it sounds when half the company only meets you in writing."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Install the handbook bookmark. Almost every process question is answered there."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not forward work documents to a personal address to read them at home. It is the single most common way company data leaks, and it is entirely avoidable."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If something will not let you in, say so on the first day rather than working around it. Access problems are five minutes for the person who can fix them and a week of quiet frustration for you."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	57	2	19	activity_978a2dcb-deb5-4f75-9bc7-22195f9d073c	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.229391	null	1	\N
Meetings, and how to survive them	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every meeting needs three things"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A reason to exist, a person responsible for it, and a written outcome. If a meeting invite arrives without those, it is entirely reasonable to reply and ask what the meeting is for. People will thank you."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Your part in them"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Read whatever was circulated beforehand. Meetings where nobody read the document become meetings where somebody reads the document aloud."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say the uncomfortable thing early. A concern raised at the end is a concern raised too late."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If you agreed to do something, write it down yourself. Do not rely on someone else's notes."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Declining a meeting you have nothing to contribute to is not rude here. Attending in silence for an hour is the more expensive option."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "70fe8660-e2d7-5de7-9b58-d3aa0fc28f3b", "questions": [{"question_id": "6d626cb0-6703-5186-a490-7dc07d110f79", "question": "You are invited to a meeting with no agenda. What is the expected response?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "3d8f607a-ecd5-5183-a02f-f205424ce775", "answer": "Reply and ask what the meeting is for", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "e3ea2c92-3386-5847-9080-fb386542187b", "answer": "Attend and hope it becomes clear", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "18c9e5c0-1a0b-5f6c-ab59-0ad124bda2d4", "answer": "Decline without saying anything", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	58	2	19	activity_b417d5a7-3731-4fd3-9fb5-653f7eb03ff4	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.237904	null	1	\N
Writing things down	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If it is not written down, it did not happen"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Riverbend runs across three sites and two time zones. A decision made in conversation and never recorded will be re-made, differently, within a month. That is not a hypothetical \\u2014 it is the single most common source of rework here."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What is worth recording"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Decisions, and crucially the reason for them. The reason is what stops the decision being reopened."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Anything a customer was promised, including dates."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Anything that surprised you, while it is still surprising."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What is not worth recording: a transcript of every conversation. Aim for the shortest note a colleague could act on in six months without asking you a follow-up question."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	59	2	19	activity_9dac001c-7cad-4cfe-b42a-1b54828eda6b	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.242013	null	1	\N
How to ask for help	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The two-hour rule"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If you have been stuck on the same thing for two hours, stop and ask. Nobody here is impressed by silent struggling, and the cost of a blocked person is much higher than the cost of a five-minute answer."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask a question people can answer"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A good request tells the other person what you were trying to do, what you tried, and what happened instead. A bad one says it is not working. The difference is roughly a day of turnaround."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What I was trying to do."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What I tried, and what I expected."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What actually happened, with the exact error or wording."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What I think might be going on, if anything."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Asking in a shared channel rather than a direct message means the answer helps the next person too \\u2014 and you are rarely the first to hit it."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "5c8a9f6b-bf21-52af-a5f0-f90524a76080", "questions": [{"question_id": "a63b0adb-0453-59a1-a251-8812f80c5cb9", "question": "How long should you stay stuck before asking for help?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "28264dfa-10fa-5d72-a7ef-b9b2283b4031", "answer": "About two hours", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "1a262695-e993-53ff-9f7a-0234d261b01d", "answer": "Until the end of the day", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "9c1d1258-19a0-5199-a0b0-ea6a9058e1eb", "answer": "Until your next one-to-one", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	60	2	19	activity_baf9be5d-bd48-4fe1-a395-34177eb064cb	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.246129	null	1	\N
Your first one-to-one	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It is your meeting, not your manager's"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The half hour is yours to spend. Managers who fill it with status updates are wasting it, and so are new starters who arrive with nothing to say. Bring two or three things you actually want addressed."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Things worth raising early"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What would a good first three months look like, specifically?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Which of the things I am confused about should I stop worrying about?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Who should I be talking to that I have not met yet?"}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask what good looks like now rather than at your first review. Expectations discovered in month three are expectations you spent two months missing."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	61	2	19	activity_862ac817-df30-46f1-9048-f9c504296b16	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.254062	null	1	\N
The mistakes everyone makes	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four you can skip"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Waiting to be given work. Nobody is holding a queue for you. Ask what would be useful and pick something up."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Nodding along to acronyms. Ask the first time and it takes ten seconds; ask in month four and it is awkward for everyone."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Promising a customer a date you have not checked. Once said, it is very hard to unsay."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Assuming everything undocumented is deliberate. Most of it is just nobody having got to it \\u2014 including things you could write up yourself."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The fourth one is an opportunity. New starters see the gaps clearly for about six weeks, and then stop noticing them like everyone else."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	62	2	19	activity_7372c397-276c-4a6e-942f-0aa3cd4a8758	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.257867	null	1	\N
Orientation check	TYPE_ASSIGNMENT	SUBTYPE_ASSIGNMENT_ANY	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Show that you have landed"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A short check covering the ground in this course: who owns what, how we record decisions, and how to ask for help well. It is marked, but it is not a trap \\u2014 everything here is answered somewhere in the three chapters above."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "There is a written question at the end asking what confused you most in your first fortnight. Answer it honestly. Those answers are what this course gets rewritten from."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	63	2	19	activity_a6e96f8f-c976-4911-8414-2b9a651c64a7	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.261744	null	1	\N
Lead with the point	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Put the ask in the first line"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Most work messages bury the request under context. The reader gets three paragraphs of background and only then discovers what they are being asked to do \\u2014 by which point they have skimmed it. Invert that. The first line says what you need and by when; the context follows for whoever wants it."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two versions of the same message"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Weak: a long explanation of a stock discrepancy, ending with a question about whether to hold the order. Strong: 'Can you confirm by Thursday whether we hold order 4192? Background below.' Same information, a fraction of the effort to act on."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One message, one ask. Two asks in one message reliably gets one answer."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Name the person you need it from. 'Someone should look at this' is a message to nobody."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Give a date. 'When you get a chance' means next month."}]}]}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "3bec61c0-d263-54aa-8dca-e98e3e819420", "questions": [{"question_id": "240bd798-101a-5935-a05b-97b65227c189", "question": "Where should the request go in a work message?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "2ae97b95-5a13-5958-acca-e834d71f22ca", "answer": "In the first line, before the context", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "54c48f78-4ad2-520f-8193-b053d03ad120", "answer": "At the end, after the reasoning", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "62426592-6678-5f7f-8935-0a19c316d0f5", "answer": "In the subject line only", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	64	2	20	activity_b0dd6db2-57ed-4d0f-95c1-6d1ffb80d9f4	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.275174	null	1	\N
Cutting it down	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Length is a cost you pass to the reader"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A message that takes you ten minutes to write and two minutes to read is a good trade when forty people read it. Writing long is easier; writing short is a courtesy."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What to cut first"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The warm-up. 'I hope this finds you well, I wanted to reach out regarding' \\u2014 delete it and start at the real first sentence."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The history. Unless the reader needs it to decide, link to it instead of retelling it."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The hedging. 'I was maybe wondering if it might be possible to perhaps' is one word: 'can'."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Anything you wrote to sound thorough rather than to be understood."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Re-read anything longer than a screen before sending. You will cut a third of it, and it will be a better message."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	65	2	20	activity_c86034eb-a41b-49a9-a1da-e42d6100c42d	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.278746	null	1	\N
Tone, and why brief is not rude	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Short messages read colder than they are"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Written text strips out everything a face and a voice provide. A three-word reply that felt efficient to you can read as annoyed to someone having a bad day. This is not a reason to pad your writing \\u2014 it is a reason to be deliberate about a few small signals."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what you appreciated when it is true. One specific sentence beats a paragraph of general warmth."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Explain a 'no' briefly. An unexplained refusal invites people to invent a reason, and the invented one is usually worse."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask rather than assert when you are not certain. 'Am I reading this right?' costs nothing and prevents a lot."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "And if a thread has gone around more than twice without converging, stop writing and talk. Some disagreements are only visible in a voice."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "a190104a-8f7c-59fb-9d67-2608ed698d92", "questions": [{"question_id": "4d911c59-b955-5575-adef-1373a9c399f1", "question": "A written thread has gone back and forth three times without agreement. What should you do?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "de03593f-d13d-5ff8-b5e4-1227a3612ac5", "answer": "Stop writing and have a conversation", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "0caff360-f7a6-5af4-9901-8d65a7c4aec0", "answer": "Write a longer, more detailed message", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "f2eb3322-256b-5ed9-8a37-ba45a2a925da", "answer": "Escalate to a manager immediately", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	66	2	20	activity_e19b3c77-7668-4a38-baaa-a691497c6996	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.281884	null	1	\N
Writing a status update	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three lines, in this order"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Where it stands, in one sentence, in plain language."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What has changed since last time, especially anything that got worse."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you need from anyone reading."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That is the whole format. It works for a project, a customer account, or a piece of work you picked up yesterday. What it does not include is a list of everything you did \\u2014 activity is not progress, and a reader cannot tell the difference from a task list."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say when things slip"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A slipped date reported early is a scheduling problem. The same date reported the day it was due is a trust problem. Nobody at Riverbend has ever been in trouble for flagging a delay in good time."}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never let a customer discover a delay from the absence of a delivery. If a date is at risk, it is told, not discovered."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	67	2	20	activity_b1fda22f-aac8-4f0b-9422-df2a27b72f30	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.288122	null	1	\N
Handing work over	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Write it for someone who was not there"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Handovers fail because the person writing them still has all the context in their head and cannot see what is missing. Assume the reader knows the product but nothing about this particular piece of work."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What the work is for, and who wanted it."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What state it is in right now, honestly, including the parts that are held together loosely."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you would do next, and what you would avoid."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Who to ask when the note runs out."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That last line is the one most people forget, and it is the one that saves the handover when everything else in it has gone stale."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	68	2	20	activity_a379be41-8630-4692-9578-6ee6d7a26a19	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.291276	null	1	\N
Delivering difficult news	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say it in the first sentence"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "There is a strong pull to soften bad news by delaying it. It does not work. The reader knows something is wrong by the second paragraph and reads the rest impatiently, or misses the point entirely and finds out later."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The shape that works"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What has happened, plainly."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What it means for them, specifically."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you are doing about it."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you need from them, if anything."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not apologise four times. One clear apology, then the plan. Repeated apology reads as anxiety and makes the reader less confident that it is under control."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If the news is genuinely serious, write the message and then call. The written version stops it being misremembered; the call stops it being read coldly."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "59ee9dc0-9c8a-5128-b30b-486490577680", "questions": [{"question_id": "37054036-89af-584f-9361-9849ff1d1070", "question": "Where does the bad news go in a difficult message?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "531e85f8-cb34-5109-bacd-fe22ad7aa5c0", "answer": "In the first sentence", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "2db0ae37-5eae-5b20-9fd4-fe115455910b", "answer": "After the context, so it lands gently", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "7466dac6-3673-553b-a08c-338d82071046", "answer": "At the very end, with the next steps", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	69	2	20	activity_c21ab6a1-4902-4ce0-bca1-019f2793fbfb	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.294348	null	1	\N
Giving feedback that lands	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Be specific about the thing, not the person"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "'This section is hard to follow because the numbers change halfway through' is useful. 'This is sloppy' is not \\u2014 there is nothing to act on in it, and the reader spends their energy on feeling bad rather than on fixing it."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A workable pattern"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Name the specific thing you are reacting to."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what effect it had on you as a reader or user."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Suggest a direction, without insisting on your version."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "And separate the strong opinions from the weak ones. If everything you say carries the same weight, people cannot tell what actually matters to you, and they will either fight all of it or none of it."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	70	2	20	activity_642db9c1-b666-41e7-8a68-920770b07f9c	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.300366	null	1	\N
Disagreeing well	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Argue about the decision, not the person who made it"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Disagreement is not a problem here; it is most of how decisions get any better. What causes damage is disagreement that becomes about competence, or that arrives so late that reversing course is expensive."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what you would do instead. Objection without an alternative is very hard to act on."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say how strongly you hold it. 'I would lean the other way' and 'I think this will fail' need different responses."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Once it is decided, commit to it properly \\u2014 including in front of people who were not in the room."}]}]}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "c961d011-4cef-59dd-95a2-f9f90f9bac00", "questions": [{"question_id": "40f275d0-fedd-5c6f-979d-ae465076e1ad", "question": "What does a useful disagreement include?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "0ed00ec9-4699-56d0-bd9d-92fecb6ef89c", "answer": "An alternative, and how strongly you hold the view", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "dc725848-7eff-5c30-81d7-999e02f52c2a", "answer": "A full account of everything wrong with the proposal", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "ffa8afef-0033-5167-8b4f-521475b16b37", "answer": "A private message to the decision-maker's manager", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	71	2	20	activity_b5faf186-ae51-4ccf-a528-f0652948ae46	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.303969	null	1	\N
Saying no	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A clear no beats a soft maybe"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Refusing a request badly costs more than refusing it at all. A customer told 'probably not, but let me check' will wait a week and then be angry about the same answer they could have had immediately."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The shape of a good refusal"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The answer, plainly: we are not able to do that."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The reason, in one sentence, in terms that affect them."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The nearest thing we can do instead."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That third step is the whole job. Almost every refusal has an adjacent yes \\u2014 a partial refund instead of a full one, a substitute item, an earlier delivery slot. Find it before you reply."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "989b6359-9d5e-5ddd-9768-949aae229b30", "questions": [{"question_id": "caa4ac54-f096-55a4-92d1-9654f97e7573", "question": "What is the most important part of refusing a customer request?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "47c0eda7-7e9a-5e33-af24-3440ae73538b", "answer": "Offering the nearest thing you can actually do", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "fe4e8ea6-376f-5ae9-815e-3e4825ea4b27", "answer": "Explaining the policy in full", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "4c7a5e53-a555-5e2d-b8ef-e589a6bb01a1", "answer": "Softening the answer so it feels less final", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	77	2	21	activity_c285cc00-ab97-4fec-ac5e-d766109ace06	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.334859	null	1	\N
When it was our mistake	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say so first, plainly"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Customers forgive errors far more readily than they forgive evasiveness. 'We shipped the wrong item and that is our error' ends the argument. 'There appears to have been a discrepancy in fulfilment' starts one."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Own it without hedging, and without blaming a named colleague or a supplier."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Fix the immediate problem before discussing compensation. Get them the thing they paid for."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what stops it happening again, only if you actually know. Inventing a fix is worse than admitting you do not have one yet."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never tell a customer that a colleague made a mistake. Riverbend made the mistake. Internally, name the process rather than the person."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	78	2	21	activity_65e6498d-6269-4d9e-aa16-6285bc5a093e	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.337781	null	1	\N
When to escalate	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four triggers, no judgement call required"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "More than one customer reports the same fault within an hour."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The customer mentions legal action, a regulator, or the press."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A refund or credit above the current threshold is on the table."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You have been going back and forth for three days without progress."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Any of those, escalate immediately. These are deliberately mechanical: they are the situations where a well-meaning attempt to handle it yourself reliably makes it worse."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Escalating is not failing"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The cost of escalating something that turned out to be simple is a few minutes of a lead's time. The cost of not escalating something serious is measured in customers. Nobody here has ever been criticised for escalating too early."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "7601d273-b617-52d3-98ce-a999e58892d0", "questions": [{"question_id": "5b464d8a-e28f-509a-b938-dbf312e2c8ed", "question": "A customer mentions they are considering legal action. What do you do?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "d5633f71-dbff-5fc3-a911-09d998254815", "answer": "Escalate immediately", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "a74639e1-168a-5a90-bbea-3f681ae5a8cc", "answer": "Try to resolve it yourself first to avoid alarming anyone", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "b76e7aa8-14ba-5faf-9f54-5dba13f1269e", "answer": "Wait to see whether they raise it again", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	79	2	21	activity_8a840210-8a34-4f85-811d-9528c883709e	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.343031	null	1	\N
Handing a case over	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The receiving person should not have to read the thread"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A handover that says 'see thread' is not a handover. Whoever picks it up is now doing your reading as well as their work, usually while the customer waits."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One line on what the customer wants."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What has been tried, and what was ruled out."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What the customer has been promised, and when."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why it is being escalated now."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That fourth line matters most. It tells the next person whether they are being asked for a decision, an authority they have and you do not, or simply a second opinion."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	80	2	21	activity_ce2c21ed-00a8-45e5-903e-c75f04047514	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.345771	null	1	\N
Support scenarios	TYPE_ASSIGNMENT	SUBTYPE_ASSIGNMENT_ANY	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four cases, four decisions"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You will work through four incoming messages of the kind that actually arrive here: an angry customer with a genuine fault, a request we cannot fulfil, a case that meets an escalation trigger, and one where the customer is mistaken but polite."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "For each, decide the priority, say whether it escalates, and draft the first reply. Marked on the escalation calls and on whether your replies contain a real commitment rather than a promise to look into it."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	81	2	21	activity_81d956c5-ad01-4f62-8502-56b8b80bd589	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.348471	null	1	\N
How the catalogue is organised	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three levels, and only three"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Everything Riverbend sells sits in a category, a family within that category, and a line within that family. A customer asking for a product by name is usually naming a family, not the line they want \\u2014 which is where most mis-shipments start."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Category: the broad area. Roughly a dozen of them, and they rarely change."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Family: a group that shares a purpose and usually a supplier."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Line: the actual thing with a code, a price and a stock level. This is what goes on an order."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why the distinction matters"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two lines in the same family can differ in lead time by three weeks. Confirming the family and shipping the wrong line is the single most common avoidable error here, and it is always caught after the delivery rather than before."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Always read the line code back to the customer before confirming an order. It takes four seconds and prevents the most expensive mistake in this course."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "5dc9758a-7f01-596a-86fb-d091ede88be7", "questions": [{"question_id": "1955abf4-396b-5e05-9bcb-97ed05f3e585", "question": "A customer names a product but not a code. What are they most likely naming?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "34d2e017-15af-5ff3-80c7-7daaacff3303", "answer": "A family, which may contain several different lines", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "c057680d-8b76-5d40-9cf7-a04909f1c7ef", "answer": "A specific line, which you can order directly", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "35e21f48-a6a9-5ddd-9151-ae1c46845841", "answer": "A category, which is too broad to order from", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	82	2	22	activity_b3dda56a-b219-40c0-832f-2514ed035d57	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.360389	null	1	\N
Reading stock levels	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Available is not the same as in stock"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The number on a line is what is physically in the warehouse. What a customer can actually have is that number minus everything already committed to other orders. Quoting the first number as though it were the second is how two customers get promised the same last unit."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "In stock: physically present, including units already spoken for."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Committed: allocated to orders that have not shipped."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Available: in stock minus committed. This is the only number worth quoting."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never promise the last available unit without checking committed stock. If two people do this on the same afternoon, one customer gets a phone call nobody wants to make."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	83	2	22	activity_426d5854-3860-4c64-acc3-012ee399e947	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.363282	null	1	\N
Suggesting a substitute	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A good substitute solves the same problem"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "When something is unavailable, the useful question is not 'what is similar?' but 'what were they going to do with it?'. Two lines can look nearly identical on paper and be useless for a particular job."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask what it is for before offering an alternative."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say plainly how the substitute differs. Discovering the difference on delivery is far worse than hearing it now."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If there is no good substitute, say so. Pushing a poor one costs a return and some trust."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Substitutions that get refused politely are fine. Substitutions that get accepted and then returned are expensive, and they are almost always the result of glossing over a difference at this stage."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	84	2	22	activity_fd6882da-9e65-4c9b-b2b6-b4a22deb1ab5	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.366410	null	1	\N
How pricing works	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "List, tier, and agreed"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three prices exist for any line and they are not interchangeable. Quoting the wrong one is not a rounding error \\u2014 it is a promise the company then has to either honour or retract."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "List: the published price. What a new customer sees."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Tier: an automatic discount based on volume over the last twelve months."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Agreed: a negotiated price on the account, which overrides both."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Always check the account before quoting. A customer on an agreed price who is quoted list will assume we are trying it on, and they will be partly right."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "9884cb58-4ada-58d4-ac79-3834c293e371", "questions": [{"question_id": "c6fe61d2-cae2-5b09-84f7-613fc9f29207", "question": "A customer has an agreed price on their account. Which price applies?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "1766034b-c2ac-5901-b0bb-55d6ac4319de", "answer": "The agreed price, which overrides list and tier", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "9c55cb48-b512-5058-ac23-aefb03e8bdfb", "answer": "Whichever is lowest of the three", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "79fb05ff-c47f-5bf5-86ec-be9971dce476", "answer": "The tier price, since it is calculated automatically", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	85	2	22	activity_780f2300-950e-4d29-99c3-641d6602b04e	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.371768	null	1	\N
Lead times, honestly	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Quote the range, not the best case"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every lead time has a typical case and a bad case. Quoting the typical one as though it were guaranteed feels helpful and generates a complaint about a fortnight later. Quote the range and say which end you expect."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What actually moves a date"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Whether the line is held in the warehouse or ordered from the supplier."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Where it is going. Some destinations add days that have nothing to do with us."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Whether the order is complete. A single unavailable line holds the whole shipment unless the customer asks to split it."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That last point is worth raising proactively. Many customers would happily take a partial delivery and never think to ask."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "c0cf07bf-fd38-5032-806e-2ca1f62fb9db", "questions": [{"question_id": "34f15f74-2760-563c-a2c5-33163fa71dc1", "question": "One line on a multi-item order is unavailable. What happens by default?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "8fae72ad-c6ce-54e3-a8ff-a8c5a65d4a24", "answer": "The whole order waits, unless the customer asks to split it", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "7ff9ad22-9d7e-5b13-9baa-90896f40d2c4", "answer": "The available items ship immediately and the rest follows", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "453c0c50-7c04-5add-94a4-aecbcd71c866", "answer": "The unavailable line is dropped from the order", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	86	2	22	activity_e443ac89-cfdf-4e3f-b9e2-93c3334492d3	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.374569	null	1	\N
What you must not promise	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four things that are not yours to give"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A price below the agreed price on the account."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A delivery date that is not in the system, however confident you feel."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Availability of a line you have not checked in the last hour."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Any commitment about a supplier's own timelines."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "These are not bureaucratic. Each one has produced a real dispute, and in every case the customer was reasonable to be annoyed \\u2014 they were told something by someone who works here, which makes it a company promise regardless of who said it."}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If you have already promised one of these by mistake, say so immediately to your team lead. Fixing it the same day is nearly always possible; fixing it after delivery is not."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	87	2	22	activity_4f4187d6-6ab4-4d09-8327-fdee52e979a7	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.377446	null	1	\N
The five recurring questions	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Learn these and you have covered most conversations"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Can I have it sooner? Sometimes, by splitting the order or paying for a faster service. Check both before saying no."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why is it more expensive than last time? Usually a tier change or an expired agreed price. Check the account before answering."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Is this the same as the one I had before? Check the line code, not the family name."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Can I return it if it is wrong? Yes, within the returns window, unless it was made to order."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do you have anything cheaper? Ask what it is for first \\u2014 the cheaper line is often unsuitable and the return costs more than the difference."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "In every one of these, the answer starts with looking something up. Answering from memory is where the errors come from."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	88	2	22	activity_2ed3f5c4-1df6-4c7a-ae78-ebf3b375e7e8	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.382905	null	1	\N
A full order, start to finish	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One order, followed all the way through"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A customer calls asking for forty units of something they describe by family name. Here is the whole path, with the decision points marked."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Identify the line. Two lines match the family; one has a three-week lead time. Read the code back before going further."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check the account. There is an agreed price, so list and tier are both irrelevant."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check available stock, not stock on hand. Twenty-eight are genuinely free."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Offer the split: twenty-eight now, twelve in three weeks. The customer takes it."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Confirm in writing, with both dates and the line code."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The order took six minutes. Five of those were checking things rather than typing, which is the correct ratio. Every error this course warns about would have been introduced by skipping one of those checks."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	89	2	22	activity_7a885d44-780a-44e3-9a83-c606eb9cafef	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.385797	null	1	\N
Catalogue and pricing check	TYPE_ASSIGNMENT	SUBTYPE_ASSIGNMENT_ANY	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Quote four orders correctly"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Four customer requests, each with an account attached. For each one, identify the correct line, work out which price applies, and give a lead time as a range."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One of the four is a trap: the customer names a family that contains two lines with very different lead times. Getting that one right is most of the mark."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	90	2	22	activity_79d562e7-99fe-4f82-af76-a5227fa1267f	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.388824	null	1	\N
What is actually being counted	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every figure has a definition, and it is rarely on the chart"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A report says orders were up eleven per cent. Before that means anything, you need to know what counts as an order. Placed, or shipped? Does a cancelled order that was placed and refunded still count? Are the two months being compared the same length?"}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three questions before you believe a number"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What exactly is in the count, and what is excluded?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Over what period, and is the comparison period genuinely comparable?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Has the definition changed since the last time this was reported?"}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That third one catches more mistakes than the other two together. A definition quietly changing between two reports produces a dramatic-looking trend that is entirely an artefact."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "34730e49-aaa0-53d1-bf5e-a3d06ffcd44e", "questions": [{"question_id": "6ed3c4da-d30c-5416-91fb-72d47642ea73", "question": "A metric jumps sharply between two months. What should you check first?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "7f23f2b5-8c95-5e6f-b063-e332faccb7b7", "answer": "Whether the definition of the metric changed", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "c110d9c0-4e49-53dc-b09d-d267e266a96c", "answer": "Whether the increase is statistically significant", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "b674ddd5-bcee-57f0-b2ef-2a448b8bd87c", "answer": "Whether the chart axis starts at zero", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	91	2	23	activity_305de3f7-bada-4ce1-a553-e290a511da73	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.400110	null	1	\N
The trouble with averages	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "An average hides the shape"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Average order value went up. That is consistent with every customer spending a little more, and equally consistent with most customers spending less while two very large orders dragged the mean upward. Those two situations call for opposite responses."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The mean is pulled around by extremes. In anything money-shaped, there are always extremes."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The median tells you about the typical case, which is usually what you actually wanted."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If mean and median are far apart, the distribution is skewed and the average is a poor summary."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask for the median alongside the mean. If the person who produced the report cannot supply it, that is itself useful information about how the report was built."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "e1071664-ba0d-5e43-9ce8-13e29b9aa06d", "questions": [{"question_id": "2cc18a6d-796b-57b7-a69a-2b46feb6663d", "question": "Mean order value rose but median order value fell. What is the likely explanation?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "e68177bc-0114-5b01-9674-3dcff1af3558", "answer": "A small number of very large orders pulled the mean up", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "aa9232e8-b829-5bda-9ec1-c23e91aafc45", "answer": "Most customers are spending more per order", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "4b483c72-1795-5af1-b83e-7e769e9e1689", "answer": "The total number of orders increased", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	92	2	23	activity_38e4781f-547f-4a3c-8513-10c2a399c5df	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.403078	null	1	\N
How charts mislead	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Usually carelessness, occasionally not"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Most misleading charts are not dishonest. They are produced quickly by someone who already knows the conclusion and is illustrating it. The effect on the reader is the same either way."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A truncated axis turns a two per cent change into a cliff."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A comparison against an unusually bad period makes anything look like recovery."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Percentages without absolute numbers hide that a hundred per cent rise was two orders becoming four."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A moving average smooths away the very spike someone needs to see."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The fix is boring and reliable: ask for the underlying numbers. Anyone producing an honest chart will hand them over without hesitating."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	93	2	23	activity_df7ef743-fec2-4add-a102-afee7ca65ca8	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.406005	null	1	\N
Making a question answerable	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "'How are we doing?' cannot be answered"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Vague questions produce vague reports that nobody acts on. The work is turning a feeling into something with a definition, a period and a comparison."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The same question, three times"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Weak: are customers happy?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Better: are complaints going up?"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Answerable: has the number of complaints per hundred shipped orders changed over the last six months, compared with the six before?"}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The third version specifies what is counted, what it is divided by, and what it is compared against. It is also the only one that produces an answer you could disagree with \\u2014 which is what makes it worth asking."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "a1c165bf-9ba6-5bca-8aba-bdb401d0697a", "questions": [{"question_id": "4a17c286-2c91-549d-bd8a-409573b08be9", "question": "What makes a question about data answerable?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "87f82d5f-c565-5c19-9291-2bb34bdf6db3", "answer": "A clear definition, a period, and a comparison", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "a134aa10-a250-5985-b8b8-f4efdaf7181e", "answer": "Access to the full dataset", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "e9588720-60d8-5b2c-9fa2-b18af07131d1", "answer": "Asking someone from the analytics team", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	94	2	23	activity_b242218c-66cb-4b57-90b5-031fe62f464d	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.411793	null	1	\N
Two things moving together	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The most expensive mistake in this course"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complaints fell in the same month a new process launched. It is very tempting to conclude the process worked. It is also the month a large seasonal customer stopped ordering, which removed most of the complaint volume by itself."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask what else changed in the same period. Something always did."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask whether the effect appeared before the supposed cause. It happens more often than you would expect."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ask whether the size of the effect is plausible for the size of the change."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You will rarely be able to prove causation from a business report, and that is fine. The goal is to stop acting confidently on a coincidence, not to run an experiment."}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Be most careful when the data agrees with you. That is when nobody in the room asks the awkward question."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	95	2	23	activity_d6927f1d-704a-40df-bb49-ace763672a06	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.414757	null	1	\N
Presenting a number honestly	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say what would change your mind"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The most credible way to present a finding is to state plainly what it does not show. It costs you nothing, and it stops someone else finding the hole and discounting the whole thing."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The number, with its definition."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The period and the comparison."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What else changed that might explain it."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you would need to be more confident."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A report structured this way survives being questioned. One that presents only the supporting evidence does not, and the questioning tends to happen in the meeting where a decision was going to be made."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	96	2	23	activity_b4fd7184-7e2a-4054-9dea-8382fd15ce4e	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.417659	null	1	\N
A worked example	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The quarterly summary, pulled apart"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A summary reports that returns are down eighteen per cent and treats it as a win. Working through it properly:"}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Definition: returns are counted when processed, not when requested. The processing backlog grew that quarter."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Period: the comparison quarter included a recall, which was unusually bad."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Absolute numbers: the fall is from 61 to 50, so eleven returns."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Other changes: total shipments also fell, so the return rate barely moved."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The honest version of the headline is that returns fell roughly in line with shipments, and some of the reduction is a backlog rather than a real improvement. That is much less exciting and considerably more useful."}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Nothing in that analysis required statistics. It required reading the definition and asking what else moved."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	97	2	23	activity_2047bf79-4330-41f3-b77e-5185201b891a	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.423284	null	1	\N
Common errors to recognise	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A short list worth memorising"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Comparing a partial period against a complete one. The current month always looks terrible on the fifth."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Averaging an average. The result is not the average of the underlying data unless the groups are the same size."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Reporting a rate without the denominator, so nobody can tell if it moved because the top or the bottom changed."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Rounding twice, so the parts no longer sum to the total and someone spends an afternoon on it."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "None of these are sophisticated. All of them have caused a wrong decision here at some point, which is why the list exists."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	98	2	23	activity_87395ab3-5bc9-48fb-9989-7c34ae58d189	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.426201	null	1	\N
Report critique	TYPE_ASSIGNMENT	SUBTYPE_ASSIGNMENT_ANY	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Find what is wrong with this report"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You will be given a one-page summary containing several of the problems in this course: a truncated axis, a metric whose definition changed, an average concealing a skew, and a causal claim resting on a coincidence."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Identify each one and say what you would ask for to check it. Marked on the problems you find and on the quality of the follow-up question \\u2014 spotting a flaw without knowing what to ask next is only half the job."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	99	2	23	activity_2c0cd939-6cc6-4f77-9d1e-290cb4f852a0	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.429197	null	1	\N
What we hold and why	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Only what the work requires"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Riverbend holds contact details, delivery addresses, order history and payment references. We do not hold full card numbers, and there is no situation in which anyone here needs one. If a customer starts reading one out, stop them."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The principle underneath all of it"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data is collected for a stated purpose and used for that purpose. An address given for delivery is not a marketing list. This is not a technicality \\u2014 it is the single rule that most of the others follow from."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Collect only what the task needs."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use it only for what it was given for."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep it only while there is a reason to."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Share it only with people who need it to do their job."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never take customer data out of company systems. That includes pasting a list into a personal spreadsheet to work on it more conveniently, which is by far the most common version of this."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "3318fe55-55fc-557c-af43-850ef905603d", "questions": [{"question_id": "2ae90f2a-fd31-5347-a52e-8d4d0d3e482f", "question": "A customer starts reading out their full card number. What do you do?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "2cecbf9b-5009-50d2-867a-bb8e451a85fd", "answer": "Stop them \\u2014 we never take full card numbers", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "b9b54b45-6139-5083-8f3f-78d60ea01c44", "answer": "Write it down and delete it after processing", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "f04f8214-252c-5b2a-a836-1053ec0a50e1", "answer": "Enter it into the order notes for the finance team", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	100	2	24	activity_e5ca7a2f-feed-4cf1-917a-fdf867b90fcc	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.441325	null	1	\N
Who may see what	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Access follows the job, not the seniority"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A team lead does not automatically get to see an account they have no involvement with, and a new starter working an account sees everything they need for it. Curiosity is not a business reason, and looking up an account you have no work on is a disciplinary matter rather than a small thing."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Look at an account because you are working on it, not because you recognise the name."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not share your login. Every action is recorded against the account that performed it, which protects you as much as anyone."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If you can see something you do not think you should, say so. Over-broad access is a fault to report, not a perk."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Access reviews happen quarterly. If your job changed, your access should have changed with it \\u2014 flag it rather than waiting for the review to catch up."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	101	2	24	activity_a759738e-17b4-442a-aa36-b65796fe86f5	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.444842	null	1	\N
When a customer asks about their data	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "They have rights, and there is a clock"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A customer may ask what we hold about them, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be deleted. These requests have legal deadlines, and the clock starts when the request arrives \\u2014 not when someone gets round to recognising it as one."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Recognise it. It will rarely use formal wording; 'what do you have on me?' counts."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Log it the same day, through the compliance channel rather than in the ticket."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not action it yourself, and do not promise a timescale on the spot."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Confirm to the customer that it has been passed on."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Deleting an account because a customer asked, without going through this process, is itself a problem: some records must be retained for accounting, and an enthusiastic deletion can breach a different obligation."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "a090f0ab-7da7-5289-8b97-7eddcdb3dcab", "questions": [{"question_id": "d7de58ea-53b2-5e54-a26b-3f66998487a1", "question": "A customer asks in a support chat what data you hold about them. What is the first step?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "aa77e3ad-835a-5bb6-a7e3-fa87ebd3b51b", "answer": "Log it as a data request the same day and pass it on", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "cc1149e8-cbb2-5fbe-8be6-bdd45ee98ebb", "answer": "Send them their order history straight away to be helpful", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "7c0eb4e8-f911-59b7-95a9-7814567698d4", "answer": "Ask them to put the request in writing by post", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	102	2	24	activity_f56dd445-7b30-4c0e-b1e6-4c920bda2cf9	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.448486	null	1	\N
What counts as a breach	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Wider than most people assume"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "People picture a breach as an attacker. Most real ones are ordinary mistakes, and they count just the same."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "An email with customer details sent to the wrong recipient."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A document shared with a link set to anyone rather than to named people."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A laptop or phone with company access lost, even briefly."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "An account left signed in on a shared machine."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Data copied somewhere it should not be, even with good intentions."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Note that four of those five are accidents by someone acting in good faith. That is the point: reporting is not an admission of wrongdoing, it is how the damage gets contained."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "5c7fc94a-65cc-5314-8ad4-53e157430716", "questions": [{"question_id": "a09c30d3-345b-58f0-a742-e70853283e57", "question": "You email an order confirmation to the wrong customer. Is this a breach?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "3130db34-7084-50ad-aeaf-3232cee8389e", "answer": "Yes \\u2014 it must be reported like any other", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "a68dfe44-c09d-5f78-9028-a3f09e2c76e8", "answer": "No, as long as you recall the message", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "88d25dfb-8aea-50bb-bf22-88644e864362", "answer": "Only if the recipient opens it", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	103	2	24	activity_f2884b4c-b273-4472-9dde-73730a0eea4b	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.455269	null	1	\N
Reporting it	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Within one hour of noticing"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The reporting window is one hour from the moment you notice, not from the moment you are sure. Riverbend has regulatory deadlines that depend on this, and they are measured from when the company first knew \\u2014 which means from when you knew."}]}, {"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What to do, in order"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Report it in the compliance channel. Do not investigate first."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not try to undo it. Recalling a message or deleting a share can destroy the evidence needed to work out the scope."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Write down what happened while it is fresh, including times."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Carry on with your day. Containment is not your job from this point."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Nobody at Riverbend has been disciplined for reporting a breach they caused. People have been disciplined for concealing one. The difference is usually a couple of hours of hesitation."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "1e6d3ec6-f7ea-5ad1-8ab1-97c38fe79c15", "questions": [{"question_id": "8c89d587-cc70-537c-a08b-3c38ccc75e25", "question": "You realise you may have shared a document too widely. What comes first?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "68bcdf0a-1b5a-5a49-9af7-933bb633a416", "answer": "Report it in the compliance channel", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "0c8c7c77-d924-5495-990f-dbde214da264", "answer": "Change the sharing settings, then report it", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "6f4dd105-c9b6-52b7-893d-5912a4778f7a", "answer": "Check who accessed it before deciding whether to report", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	104	2	24	activity_5816faad-4df0-42b2-93af-87ada1908aa5	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.458854	null	1	\N
Recognising a scam	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The ones that work look ordinary"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The attempts that succeed here are not obviously fraudulent emails. They are a supplier asking to update their bank details, or an urgent message that appears to come from someone senior asking for a payment to be made quickly and quietly."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Any change to payment details is verified by phoning a number you already had, never one in the message."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Urgency plus secrecy is the signature of this kind of fraud. Treat the combination as the alarm itself."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Seniority is not authority in this context. A request that skips the normal process is suspect regardless of who appears to have sent it."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Verifying costs a phone call and mild awkwardness. Not verifying has cost other companies a great deal of money, and the person who processed the payment was following instructions in every case."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "6d9f4ede-07a1-5efa-94b1-65fb96d48253", "questions": [{"question_id": "708ee129-db4b-504a-9f43-92b9fbd75843", "question": "A supplier emails asking to update their bank details. How do you verify?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "68656c4e-afb6-5a7f-8920-649ac41a0081", "answer": "Phone them on a number you already held, not one from the email", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "e6af1858-6072-5dbe-9705-0abe2b46ec43", "answer": "Reply to the email asking them to confirm", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "6843a253-9a35-5f98-a7ab-a2168af568d4", "answer": "Check the sender address matches previous emails", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	105	2	24	activity_bddd1044-8869-495b-9faf-7275c50b98b3	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.462339	null	1	\N
Approval thresholds	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Know the two that apply to you"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Most people only need to remember two numbers: the value above which a discount needs a second signature, and the value above which a refund does. Both are in the handbook and both change occasionally, so check rather than remember."}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Below the threshold: your decision, recorded as usual."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Above it: a second named person approves before you commit to anything with the customer."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Never split a request into two smaller ones to stay underneath. That is treated as deliberate circumvention, and it is obvious in the records."}]}]}]}, {"type": "calloutInfo", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Approval is about having a second pair of eyes, not about distrust. The threshold exists because single-person decisions above a certain size are where errors become expensive."}]}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	106	2	24	activity_4a3e45d9-dcba-4544-abaf-a35404359656	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.469101	null	1	\N
When you are asked to bend a rule	TYPE_DYNAMIC	SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It will be reasonable-sounding and urgent"}], "attrs": {"level": 2}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Nobody will ask you to do something obviously wrong. You will be asked to skip a check because a customer is waiting, or to approve something now and record it later. The pressure is usually genuine and the request is still not acceptable."}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Say plainly that you cannot do it that way."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Offer the version you can do, including how long it takes."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If the pressure continues, say you are going to check with compliance \\u2014 and then do."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Write down what was asked and by whom, the same day."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That last step protects you. If a decision is later questioned, the difference between a note written on the day and a recollection months later is considerable."}]}, {"type": "calloutWarning", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If you are asked to keep a request off the record, that fact alone is worth reporting, whatever the request was."}]}, {"type": "blockQuiz", "attrs": {"quizId": "645f5443-318c-5481-92fd-9457452f5fbb", "questions": [{"question_id": "ec2bdf55-ee1f-5f87-a172-6593c142fea8", "question": "You are pressed to approve something above your threshold because a customer is waiting. What do you do?", "type": "multiple_choice", "answers": [{"answer_id": "34b377f9-de0c-5d56-a3fd-9ac5409b48b6", "answer": "Decline, offer the compliant option, and record the request", "correct": true}, {"answer_id": "b482d801-3e43-54c8-9c24-ad73c8f6fe68", "answer": "Approve it and get the second signature afterwards", "correct": false}, {"answer_id": "c6de40e6-094d-5560-9e8d-60af8cbd3919", "answer": "Split it into two smaller approvals", "correct": false}]}]}}]}	null	t	PUBLIC	107	2	24	activity_bda819f0-aff4-45be-a7fe-cad0f35a4f58	2026-07-23 10:00:00	2026-10-01 23:52:50.472454	null	1	\N
\.


